    "created_at": "2017-06-02T11:35:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-06-02T11:35:46Z",
    "body": "IIRC, this comes from Hixie trying to spec the behavior of Gecko. I don't know if Gecko has since changed or if the spec was wrong to begin with. But in any case, I don't see any particular reason to have this like the spec currently requires.\r\n\r\nI suppose there should be two separate things here, then: (1) the current algorithm, but run it even for display:none and don't re-run it when \"being rendered\" changes, and (2) a separate algorithm to invoke and kill plugins, based on \"being rendered\". Is that closer to what Gecko does?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
