    "created_at": "2024-02-22T02:51:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-02-22T02:51:52Z",
    "body": "Just noticed that Safari now does even this reloading when the `position` of the `<object>` element is changed to `absolute`. https://jsfiddle.net/hx1eautp/ I remember they didn't always do that and I'm not sure it follows the *being rendered* definition (the element still has a box, even if maybe not the same).  \r\n\r\nBut it seems that as of today only Safari does this reload on *being rendered*, and not even as per the specs text: in case of `display: none`, they unload the attached document only when the `<object>` is rendered again, which is the behavior specced for `<embed>` https://jsfiddle.net/wuL4y73f/.  \r\n\r\nI was considering simply opening an issue at WebKit regarding the `position` stuff, but it might actually be better to fix the specs first to match the majority and adopt the same behavior as `<iframe>` expose, i.e. no reload based on *being rendered*.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
